{"id":9321,"date":"2021-10-06T12:38:18","date_gmt":"2021-10-06T12:38:18","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/solutions\/industrial-applications\/classification-of-polyethylene-using-raman-spectroscopy\/"},"modified":"2021-10-06T12:38:31","modified_gmt":"2021-10-06T12:38:31","slug":"classification-of-polyethylene-using-raman-spectroscopy","status":"publish","type":"page","link":"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/en\/solutions\/industrial-applications\/classification-of-polyethylene-using-raman-spectroscopy\/","title":{"rendered":"Classification of polyethylene using Raman spectroscopy"},"content":{"rendered":"\t\t<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-page\" data-elementor-id=\"9321\" class=\"elementor elementor-9321 elementor-9197\" data-elementor-post-type=\"page\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<section class=\"elementor-section elementor-top-section elementor-element elementor-element-5441e79 elementor-section-boxed elementor-section-height-default elementor-section-height-default\" data-id=\"5441e79\" data-element_type=\"section\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-container elementor-column-gap-default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-column elementor-col-100 elementor-top-column elementor-element elementor-element-e4d3fd5\" data-id=\"e4d3fd5\" data-element_type=\"column\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-865fb00 elementor-widget elementor-widget-eael-adv-tabs\" data-id=\"865fb00\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"eael-adv-tabs.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t        <div data-scroll-on-click=\"no\" data-scroll-speed=\"300\" id=\"eael-advance-tabs-865fb00\" class=\"eael-advance-tabs eael-tabs-horizontal eael-tab-auto-active  active-caret-on responsive-vertical-layout\" data-tabid=\"865fb00\">\n            <div class=\"eael-tabs-nav\">\n                <ul class=\"\" role=\"tablist\">\n                                            <li id=\"application-description\" class=\"inactive eael-tab-item-trigger eael-tab-nav-item\" aria-selected=\"true\" data-tab=\"1\" role=\"tab\" tabindex=\"0\" aria-controls=\"application-description-tab\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n                            \n                            \n                            \n                                                            <span class=\"eael-tab-title title-after-icon\" >Application description<\/span>                                                    <\/li>\n                                            <li id=\"raman-spectroscopy\" class=\"inactive eael-tab-item-trigger eael-tab-nav-item\" aria-selected=\"false\" data-tab=\"2\" role=\"tab\" tabindex=\"-1\" aria-controls=\"raman-spectroscopy-tab\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n                            \n                            \n                            \n                                                            <span class=\"eael-tab-title title-after-icon\" >Raman spectroscopy<\/span>                                                    <\/li>\n                                            <li id=\"ft-ir-spectroscopy\" class=\"inactive eael-tab-item-trigger eael-tab-nav-item\" aria-selected=\"false\" data-tab=\"3\" role=\"tab\" tabindex=\"-1\" aria-controls=\"ft-ir-spectroscopy-tab\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n                            \n                            \n                            \n                                                            <span class=\"eael-tab-title title-after-icon\" >FT-IR spectroscopy<\/span>                                                    <\/li>\n                                    <\/ul>\n            <\/div>\n            \n            <div class=\"eael-tabs-content\">\n\t\t        \n                    <div id=\"application-description-tab\" class=\"clearfix eael-tab-content-item inactive\" data-title-link=\"application-description-tab\">\n\t\t\t\t        <p><strong>Raman spectroscopy<\/strong> provides sample information at the molecular level, which can be used to advantage in the analysis of various types of polyethylene. This method requires almost no sample treatment, is <strong>fast, non-destructive<\/strong> and, with the help of the <a href=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/en\/application-support\/software\/tq-analyst-9\/\"><strong>TQ Analyst<\/strong><\/a> program, it is possible to perform quantitative measurements for almost every application.<\/p>\n<p>Polyethylene (PE) is currently one of the most produced plastics in the world. According to density, they are divided into low-density (LDPE) and high-density (HDPE) polyethylene, which have fundamentally different physical, chemical and mechanical properties, and therefore also the way they are used. While HDPE is mainly used for the production of various containers and tubes, LDPE is the starting material for the production of bags and similar packaging.<\/p>\n<figure id=\"attachment_9202\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-9202\" style=\"width: 800px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-9202 size-large\" src=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/10\/db28058a-1024x436.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"800\" height=\"341\" srcset=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/10\/db28058a-1024x436.png 1024w, https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/10\/db28058a-300x128.png 300w, https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/10\/db28058a-768x327.png 768w, https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/10\/db28058a-1536x654.png 1536w, https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/10\/db28058a.png 1920w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-9202\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Raman spectra of individual types of PE and spectral regions typical for them<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<p>Both types of polyethylene are produced in the form of pellets, which are then further processed into films or tubes. Their density is conventionally measured by density gradient or ultrasound, but these techniques require PE in its pure form, which can be e.g. in the case of films a problem. Therefore, it is appropriate to combine traditional methods with Raman spectroscopy &#8211; with a <a href=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/en\/product\/dxr3-microscope\/\">Nicolet DXR3<\/a> or <a href=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/en\/product\/dxr3xi-microscope\/\">DXR3xi<\/a> microscope.<\/p>\n<p>With the help of it it is possible not only to determine the chemical composition of the analyzed substance, but also to determine its concentration, or conformational changes, changes in bonds and other parameters that can facilitate and streamline production. In addition, with <strong>TQ Analyst<\/strong>you can create methods that can be used to easily and quickly distinguish between different types of PE.<\/p>\n<figure id=\"attachment_9200\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-9200\" style=\"width: 450px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-9200\" src=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/10\/0f707bca-1-300x256.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"450\" height=\"384\" srcset=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/10\/0f707bca-1-300x256.png 300w, https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/10\/0f707bca-1-768x655.png 768w, https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/10\/0f707bca-1.png 881w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 450px) 100vw, 450px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-9200\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">TQ Analyst Program: A graph of discriminant analysis that shows the distribution of individual types of PE based on spectral properties<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n                    <\/div>\n\t\t        \n                    <div id=\"raman-spectroscopy-tab\" class=\"clearfix eael-tab-content-item inactive\" data-title-link=\"raman-spectroscopy-tab\">\n\t\t\t\t        <style>@media(max-width:1024px){.elementor-6769 .elementor-element.elementor-element-8179397 .dce-post-item{padding:0px 0px 20p